    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneIV_13.4/p@152301",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "QUEEN MARGARET.\n[Aside.] Oft have I heard that grief softens the mind\nAnd makes it fearful and degenerate;\nThink therefore on revenge and cease to weep.\nBut who can cease to weep and look on this?\nHere may his head lie on my throbbing breast;\nBut where’s the body that I should embrace?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [
        {
          "tag": "i",
          "start": 17,
          "end": 22
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
